From 25289418679225e3fec5307b06be01fc1587bf6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:14:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Trilinos: the numerical type of mfem-mgis

The interface between mfem-mgis and the library MFEMMGISTrilinos uses the
numerical type of mfem-mgis (trilinos::real, given by the compile
definition MFEM_MGIS_TRILINOS_REAL_TYPE) instead of double, as the
scalar type of Tpetra and of the solvers. The configuration no longer
refuses float: it checks that Tpetra is instantiated for the numerical
type of MFEM (HAVE_TPETRA_INST_FLOAT or HAVE_TPETRA_INST_DOUBLE). Not
tested in float (Trilinos of the prototype instantiated for double only).

The reals of the parameters of mfem-mgis, kept in double precision, are
converted to the type of the reals of the parameters of Belos when it
differs (float in single precision), Teuchos requiring the exact type of
the parameters. The configuration header of Tpetra is searched in the
installation of Trilinos (Trilinos_INCLUDE_DIRS being deprecated), and
its absence is reported as such.

The GPUs of AMD (HIP) were already handled by the module (default node
of Tpetra, conversion of the matrices by kernels of Kokkos); not tested.
